Rationale: The claim states that the sub-units using two types of RNA are major components of the unit consisting of Ribosomal protein. While evidence supports that ribosomes are composed of ribosomal RNA (rRNA) and ribosomal proteins, forming small and large subunits, the specific sub-units that use two types of RNA remain insufficiently addressed. The evidence does not clarify what these two types of RNA are or how they are used by the sub-units. Further investigation is needed to confirm this part of the claim.
